1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,930
If the Moon vanished tonight, tides would

2
00:00:01,930 --> 00:00:03,060
shrink to about a third.

3
00:00:03,460 --> 00:00:05,040
Relax, it's only a thought experiment.

4
00:00:05,460 --> 00:00:06,980
Here's what scientists say would happen.

5
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:09,919
First, nights get darker, like a new moon

6
00:00:09,919 --> 00:00:11,040
every single night.

7
00:00:11,620 --> 00:00:13,160
But the tides are the big one.

8
00:00:13,580 --> 00:00:14,900
The Moon does most of the pulling.

9
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:17,598
The Sun makes tides too, but it pulls less

10
00:00:17,598 --> 00:00:18,540
than half as hard.

11
00:00:18,880 --> 00:00:21,206
So every tide would be roughly a third of

12
00:00:21,206 --> 00:00:21,660
today's.

13
00:00:21,700 --> 00:00:23,200
But animals would get confused.

14
00:00:23,700 --> 00:00:25,340
Some dung beetles steer by moonlight.

15
00:00:25,700 --> 00:00:27,328
They'd have to switch to steering by the

16
00:00:27,328 --> 00:00:28,060
Milky Way instead.

17
00:00:28,060 --> 00:00:30,120
But the strangest part is slow.

18
00:00:30,600 --> 00:00:32,812
Over a few hundred thousand years, Earth's

19
00:00:32,812 --> 00:00:33,760
tilt could wobble.

20
00:00:34,240 --> 00:00:35,280
Mars has no big moon...

21
00:00:35,840 --> 00:00:38,080
and its tilt swings by up to 60 degrees.

22
00:00:38,980 --> 00:00:39,980
Subscribe for more.

